		(property "Datasheet" "https://www.apmemory.com/cn/downloadFiles/032411212009597427"
			(at 0 25.4 0)
			(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide)
		)
		(property "Description" "8MB QSPI PSRAM, USON-8L (3x2mm) -- same CS/SCLK/SIO0-3/VCC/GND pin map as a standard SOIC-8 QSPI flash (verified against Pimoroni Pico Plus 2 published schematic), but NOT the same physical footprint: AP Memory's -ZR suffix is USON-8L, not SOIC-8 (confirmed via LCSC distributor listing C3040877). Footprint is KiCad's stock closest-match by body size (3x2mm); AP Memory's own mechanical drawing/pad geometry was not independently re-verified -- flag for PCB-layout-stage review. Pin 9/\"EP\" (pilink-2ar) was added to map the footprint's real copper exposed/thermal pad (Package_SON:Winbond_USON-8-1EP's pad \"9\", F.Cu+F.Mask, pad_prop_heatsink) and is tied to GND on the schematic -- grounding an exposed thermal/die-attach pad is the common, conventional-safe default for this package class, though similar parts' datasheets vary between calling for GND and leaving it floating/NC (e.g. Winbond's own USON-8-1EP flash family guidance is GND-or-floating, not a hard requirement to ground it), and GND is preferred absent contrary guidance; no distributor/datasheet source reachable from this agent environment (AP Memory's own PDF is not text-extractable here; Mouser-hosted mirrors of the APS6404L family datasheet timed out on fetch) gave a contradicting spec either way for this exact -3SQR-ZR part -- flag for human re-verification against AP Memory's real mechanical drawing before fab, same caveat class as the footprint-match gap above. The footprint's OTHER unlabeled centre pad (paste-only, F.Paste layer only, no F.Cu) is intentionally left with no net: it carries no copper at all, so it cannot be part of any net in KiCad and is not a defect -- it is a stencil-aperture pad purely for solder-paste deposition, same convention used elsewhere in this footprint family."
			(at 0 27.94 0)
			(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide)
		)
